    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 687ee194a32718657010b762672bc7e2eb2065b1 -->\nReviewed at head 687ee194a3. Built locally in a worktree, merged with current main; the merge is clean.\n\n**Result: clean.**\n\n- The change: `G86` always carries `P` in grblHAL.cps and tormach.cps; `P0` when the dwell is zero. `G82` and `G89` keep the old `dwell > 0` guard.\n- The claim matches the LinuxCNC G86 form: the dwell word is part of the cycle block; omitting it is refused by the interpreter.\n- I ran `bore_cycle` on the merged tree: 9/9 pass, the goldens included.\n- Law: `Changelog:` and `Fixes #2362` present; `docs/decisions/2362-g86-zero-dwell.md` in the PR; only the two posts, their tests and goldens move.\n\nThe two changed golden lines (`... R2 P0 F120`) are the whole output delta on the affected streams.\n",
